.TH tkutest n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutest
.PP
Drive a Tk user interface from a test, in the same interpreter: type, press keys, click, choose from comboboxes and menus, and answer modal dialogs. Keys and clicks are generated with \fBevent generate\fR, so the application's own bindings, validation and dialog code run as they do for a user.
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutest
namespace import ::tkutils::tkutest::*

type .form.name {Rose, rot}           ;# key events per character
key .form.name <Return>                ;# one event
click .buttons.save                    ;# Enter, Motion, Press, Release
click .list -double 1                  ;# double click
select .form.art Rechnung              ;# readonly combobox + <<ComboboxSelected>>
check .form.aktiv 0                    ;# checkbutton off
menuInvoke .m "Datei/Firmendaten…"     ;# entry by its labels
treeSelect .main.list RE-2026-0001     ;# by text, value or -column
visible .buttons.primary               ;# completely inside its toplevel?
.CE
.SS "Modal dialogs"
.PP
A modal dialog waits in \fBvwait\fR until it is closed, so the test cannot act after opening it. \fBanswer\fR registers a handler \fBbefore\fR the action; it runs inside the dialog's event loop once a new toplevel with a matching title is mapped:
.CS
set t [answer -title "Neuer Kunde" -fields {kundennr K1 name {Quarz KG}}]
fa::kundeNeu                       ;# opens the form, returns after OK
result $t                          ;# {window .tkudialog3 title {Neuer Kunde} button OK}
.CE
.TS
l l.
option	meaning
\fB\-title glob\fR	title of the dialog to wait for (default \fB*\fR)
\fB\-fields dict\fR	tkuform fields to fill (entries are cleared and typed, combos selected, checkbuttons set)
\fB\-button id\fR	tkudialog button id (\fBok\fR, \fBcancel\fR, \fByes\fR …), a button label or a path tail; \fB""\fR presses nothing
\fB\-script cmd\fR	called with the dialog path, e.g. to type into an input dialog
\fB\-timeout ms\fR	how long to wait for the dialog (default 5000)
.TE
.PP
Several \fBanswer\fR calls queue up and handle one dialog each, in order: a form and the error message it leads to, for example. \fBresult\fR returns what the handler did or raises its error (\fBTIMEOUT\fR if no such dialog appeared); \fBpending\fR lists the tokens not handled yet — at the end of a test it should be empty.
.PP
\fBanswerFile ?\-title glob? ?\-timeout ms? path\fR answers Tk's file dialog: the file name is typed into its name field and taken with Return.
.PP
Posted menus, combobox lists and tooltips (override\-redirect windows) are no dialogs: \fBtoplevels\fR, \fBwaitWindow\fR and \fBanswer \-title *\fR skip them.
.SS "Unexpected dialogs"
.PP
\fBguard ?\-after ms?\fR (default 8000) watches for a modal dialog that no handler takes. After that time it records its title and text, sends Escape and, if that does not close it, destroys it; so a test fails instead of hanging. \fBunexpected\fR returns the recorded \fB{title text}\fR pairs and clears them, \fBunguard\fR stops watching.
.SS Typing
.PP
ASCII characters are sent as KeyPress/KeyRelease. A character the active keyboard map has no key for (an umlaut on a US map, the euro sign) is inserted at the insert cursor, as an input method would. For real keyboard input through the X server use \fBtkutils::tkuxdo\fR.
.SS Waiting
.PP
\fBwait script ?\-timeout ms?\fR processes events until the expression is true; \fBwaitWindow ?\-title glob? ?\-after list?\fR returns the first new toplevel. Both raise \fB{TKUTILS TKUTEST TIMEOUT}\fR.
.SS Commands
.TS
l l.
command	does
\fBtype w text\fR	key events per character into \fBw\fR (focus first)
\fBkey w sequence\fR	one event, e.g. \fB<Return>\fR, \fB<Control\-s>\fR
\fBclear w\fR	empty an entry, combobox or text widget
\fBclick w ?\-x? ?\-y? ?\-button n? ?\-double 0/1?\fR	Enter, Motion, Press, Release; centre by default
\fBselect combo value\fR	set a combobox and send \fB<<ComboboxSelected>>\fR; \fBVALUE\fR if no choice
\fBcheck w ?value?\fR	set a checkbutton on (1) or off (0) by clicking it if needed
\fBmenuInvoke menu path\fR	invoke an entry by its labels, \fB"Datei/Öffnen…"\fR
\fBtreeItem tree text ?\-column c?\fR	item id by text, a value or one column; \fBITEM\fR if none
\fBtreeSelect tree text ?\-column c?\fR	as \fBtreeItem\fR, then show, select and focus it
\fBfindButton top label\fR	a button below \fBtop\fR by its \fB\-text\fR or path tail
\fBfill form fields\fR	fill a tkuform: entries cleared and typed, combos selected, checkbuttons set
\fBvisible w\fR	1 if \fBw\fR is mapped and lies completely inside its toplevel
\fBanswer ?options?\fR	handler for the next dialog, returns a token (see above)
\fBanswerFile ?\-title? ?\-timeout? path\fR	answer Tk's file dialog with \fBpath\fR
\fBresult token ?\-timeout ms?\fR	what the handler did, or its error
\fBpending\fR	tokens not handled yet
\fBguard ?\-after ms?\fR, \fBunguard\fR	watch for, and stop watching for, unexpected dialogs
\fBunexpected\fR	\fB{title text}\fR of the dialogs \fBguard\fR closed; clears the list
\fBwait expr ?\-timeout ms?\fR	process events until \fBexpr\fR is true
\fBwaitWindow ?\-title glob? ?\-after list? ?\-timeout ms?\fR	the first new toplevel
\fBtoplevels\fR	mapped toplevels without menus, combobox lists and tooltips
.TE
.PP
Errors: \fB{TKUTILS TKUTEST <REASON>}\fR (TIMEOUT, VALUE, MENU, ITEM, BUTTON, FORM, TOKEN, OPTION). Not in the umbrella: a test requires it directly.
